<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila C. Bank sells dlrs at 26.40 pesos-traders. [corrected 01:25 gmt]</title>
<headline>Manila C. Bank sells dlrs at 26.40 pesos-traders. [corrected 01:25 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects exchange rate in headline from 26.340.)</p>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank was selling dollars at 26.40 pesos in initial trades on Monday, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the Central Bank was a dominant seller in the market.</p>
<p>&quot;We hear there was an offshore bank trying to satisfy clients' requirements,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>The peso had so far traded at 26.40 pesos to the dollar from a previous 26.399. Volume was at $117 million.</p>
</text>
